From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:35:09 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: ipu-bridge: Map SSDB VCM type 0x11 to dw9800k

The rear OV13858 (OVTID858) of the Microsoft Surface Pro 9 reports VCM
type 0x11 in its SSDB. ipu_vcm_types[] only knows types 1 to 9, so the
bridge warns "Unknown VCM type 17", drops the VCM and the sensor gets no
lens-focus link.

On this machine the type 0x11 VCM works with the dw9719 driver's
DW9800K configuration: it binds at the VCM address of the SSDB, focus
values written through it read back from the VCM registers, and the
image changes as the lens moves over DAC codes 400 to 800. The dw9719
driver handles the DW9800K with a fixed configuration, as the part has
no ID register.

Index ipu_vcm_types[] by the SSDB value instead of value - 1, so the
table can have holes, add type 17 as "dw9800k", and treat any type
without a name as unknown. The bound check becomes ">=" accordingly.

Signed-off-by: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c | 24 +++++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c
index 2263722f5..4c0bce6d7 100644
--- a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c
+++ b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c
@@ -248,15 +248,16 @@ static const struct ipu_property_names prop_names = {
 };
 
 static const char * const ipu_vcm_types[] = {
-	"ad5823",
-	"dw9714",
-	"ad5816",
-	"dw9719",
-	"dw9718",
-	"dw9806b",
-	"wv517s",
-	"lc898122xa",
-	"lc898212axb",
+	[1] = "ad5823",
+	[2] = "dw9714",
+	[3] = "ad5816",
+	[4] = "dw9719",
+	[5] = "dw9718",
+	[6] = "dw9806b",
+	[7] = "wv517s",
+	[8] = "lc898122xa",
+	[9] = "lc898212axb",
+	[17] = "dw9800k",
 };
 
 /*
@@ -485,7 +486,8 @@ int ipu_bridge_parse_ssdb(struct acpi_device *adev, struct ipu_sensor *sensor)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	if (ssdb.vcmtype > ARRAY_SIZE(ipu_vcm_types)) {
+	if (ssdb.vcmtype >= ARRAY_SIZE(ipu_vcm_types) ||
+	    (ssdb.vcmtype && !ipu_vcm_types[ssdb.vcmtype])) {
 		dev_warn(ADEV_DEV(adev), "Unknown VCM type %d\n", ssdb.vcmtype);
 		ssdb.vcmtype = 0;
 	}
@@ -502,7 +504,7 @@ int ipu_bridge_parse_ssdb(struct acpi_device *adev, struct ipu_sensor *sensor)
 	sensor->orientation = ipu_bridge_parse_orientation(adev);
 
 	if (ssdb.vcmtype)
-		sensor->vcm_type = ipu_vcm_types[ssdb.vcmtype - 1];
+		sensor->vcm_type = ipu_vcm_types[ssdb.vcmtype];
 
 	return 0;
 }
